# oracle: pair_style meam diamond/zincblende Si-C alloy with the real library.meam + SiC.meam (zbl default 1, no pair inside the blend region), 2x2x2 conventional cells of 8 atoms (64 atoms, Si on the first sublattice, C on the second), lattice constant 4.359739 A = 4 re(1,2)/sqrt(3), 0.02 A sinusoidal displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 30 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: the parameter file sets rho0(2) = 2.25, which overwrites the library rozero = 2.25 of C; the library Si entry has rozero = 1, so this case exercises the element density scaling (docs.lammps.org/pair_meam.html "rho0(I) = relative density for element I (overwrites value read from meamf file)")
# oracle-potentials: library.meam SiC.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-9
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
variable        a equal 4.359739
lattice         diamond ${a}
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 1 1 basis 2 1 basis 3 1 basis 4 1 basis 5 2 basis 6 2 basis 7 2 basis 8 2
mass            1 28.086
mass            2 12.011
variable        dx atom 0.02*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.02*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.02*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * library.meam Si C SiC.meam Si C
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe ke press pxx pyy pzz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             30
